    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'complaint' (noun) can refer to both the feeling of discontent/dissatisfaction and a formal or specific statement of grievance. While 不平 (fuhei) aligns well with the former (discontent, grumbling), it is narrower and less commonly used for a formal 'complaint' or 'grievance' as a specific item or statement. 苦情 (kujō) is a more natural and standard term for a general 'complaint' or 'grievance', especially in contexts like customer service or formal objections, covering a broader range of the English lemma's meaning.",
